@startuml target_follow_up_handoff
skinparam backgroundColor white
' Target-only. Direction accepted; disabled in the current product.
' Source: pi-mono-java@dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/session/RuntimeSessionControlService.java
' Symbols: acceptLocked, requireRunningHolder, queueControl. Observed behavior: local Holder queues.
' Source: pi-mono@5cd93f688aaab89dbb6dfa4aca535f21796ae185
' packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts: runLoop. Observed behavior: follow-up continues the same loop.
' Design reason: durable application handoff avoids sticky routing and live output relay.
title Future FollowUp - durable handoff, not enabled
actor "Caller via Mate" as Caller
participant "Instance A\nM1 execution" as A
database "Shared database\nqueue + execution authority" as DB
participant "Instance B\nM2 application service" as B
participant "B batch dispatcher" as Watch
Caller -> A: POST Events M1
A -> DB: Accept M1 and claim execution
A --> Caller: M1 receipt and output
Caller -> B: Future queue submission M2
note over Caller, B: Public queue fields and activation require review
B -> DB: Short transaction: accept ordered pending M2
DB --> B: Committed association
B --> Caller: M2 receipt first; keep its own SSE
B -> Watch: Register local pending M2, then recheck
note over B, Watch: M2 credentials remain only in B memory
A -> DB: Commit recoverable context + real terminal + release
A --> Caller: M1 terminal; close M1 SSE only
loop Bounded instance-level batches
Watch -> DB: Read predecessor completion and queue head
DB --> Watch: Authoritative committed state
end
Watch -> B: Eligible candidate, not final admission
B -> DB: Short transaction: recheck head and atomically claim M2
DB --> B: One winning internal execution identity
B -> DB: Restore internal model context after claim
note over B, DB: Never restore from public ListEvents
B -> B: Start M2 using its own credentials
B --> Caller: M2 output on M2 SSE only
B -> DB: Commit M2 real completion
B --> Caller: M2 terminal; close M2 SSE
note over A, B
  No cross-instance Java object transfer or token relay.
  Lost owner or credentials require a separate recovery protocol.
  A lease expiry is not proof that remote side effects stopped.
end note
@enduml

@startuml target_follow_up_classes
skinparam backgroundColor white
' All types and relations below are target-only; names are not frozen.
' Source: pi-mono-java@dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java
' Symbols: register, find, createHolder. Observed behavior: process-local execution objects.
' Design reason: application-level queue authority stays separate from runtime and request credentials.
title Future FollowUp - target-only responsibility boundaries
hide empty members
package "Web / API" {
  class EventsController <<singleton, target-only>>
}
package "Application" {
  class EventSubmissionService <<singleton, target-only>>
  class FollowUpQueueService <<singleton, target-only>>
  class FollowUpDispatcher <<singleton per instance, target-only>>
  class PendingSubmissionRegistry <<singleton per instance, target-only>>
  interface FollowUpQueueRepository <<target-only>>
}
package "Persistence adapter" {
  class MyBatisFollowUpQueueRepository <<singleton, target-only>>
  class "Shared database\nqueue / claim authority" as DB <<durable store>>
}
package "Runtime boundary" {
  interface RuntimeExecutionLauncher <<target-only>>
  interface SessionContextRestorer <<target-only>>
}
EventsController --> EventSubmissionService
EventSubmissionService --> FollowUpQueueService : admit / convert VO and DTO
EventSubmissionService --> PendingSubmissionRegistry : register after commit
FollowUpDispatcher --> PendingSubmissionRegistry : bounded local candidates
FollowUpDispatcher --> FollowUpQueueService : recheck and claim
FollowUpQueueService --> FollowUpQueueRepository : transactional authority
MyBatisFollowUpQueueRepository ..|> FollowUpQueueRepository
MyBatisFollowUpQueueRepository --> DB : Mapper / DTO
FollowUpDispatcher --> RuntimeExecutionLauncher : launch only after claim
RuntimeExecutionLauncher --> SessionContextRestorer : internal durable projection
SessionContextRestorer --> DB
note bottom of FollowUpQueueService
  Revalidate mutable state inside the claim transaction.
  No network IO or model calls while holding DB locks.
end note
note right of EventsController
  RequestVO / ResponseVO only at the API boundary.
  All shown types and relations are target-only.
end note
@enduml

@startuml target_follow_up_local_lifecycle
skinparam backgroundColor white
' Target-only local lifecycle, no public queue API or durable credentials.
' Source: pi-mono-java@dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238
' campusclaw/src/main/java/com/huawei/hicampus/claw/codingagent/runtimeapi/runtime/RuntimeSessionEngineRegistry.java
' Observed behavior: registry holds local execution objects only.
' Design reason: bound pending capacity and keep request credentials out of persistence.
title Future FollowUp - local lifecycle, not enabled
hide empty members
class PendingSubmissionRegistry <<singleton, target-only>>
class PendingSubmission <<pending / execution, target-only>>
class CredentialSnapshot <<memory only, target-only>>
class BoundedResponseBuffer <<HTTP response, target-only>>
interface RuntimeExecutionLauncher <<target-only>>
class SessionExecution <<execution, target-only>>
interface ExecutionIO <<runtime port, target-only>>
PendingSubmissionRegistry "1" *-- "0..bounded" PendingSubmission
PendingSubmission "1" *-- "1" CredentialSnapshot
PendingSubmission "1" *-- "0..1" BoundedResponseBuffer
PendingSubmission ..|> ExecutionIO
RuntimeExecutionLauncher ..> SessionExecution : create after claim
SessionExecution --> ExecutionIO
note bottom of PendingSubmission
  Disconnect detaches output, not accepted work.
  Credentials are cleared at final cleanup.
  Process loss requires a separate authorization policy.
end note
@enduml
